      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "Polarized Schur orthogonality computes P on σ. Haar inversion and convolution give the adjoint and compression identities in π. Evaluating the latter at 1 gives idempotence. Orthogonality turns ⟨η,Pη⟩ into ‖Pη‖². The independent circle computation evaluates the same identity by Fourier averaging.",
      "review": "A second reader checked the kernel conjugation, the middle translation identity, the use of orthogonality in the norm formula, and the 1/5 circle calculation."
    },
    {
