      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "The same compact highest weight realizes the two vectors in an irreducible common type E. Vanishing of the projection propagates to all the mixed coefficient integrals there. Their finite trace sum is nonnegative after Cartan decomposition, and at 1 is the strictly positive squared Hilbert–Schmidt norm of the first map from E. The stronger definite-partner statement is quoted from the normalized local theorem.",
      "review": "A second reader independently checked the positivity contradiction, the nonnegative Haar integral, and its positive value at the identity."
