    {
      "id": "FPR-03",
      "title": "The cover integral in the real-place Haar normalization",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-fock-measure",
      "statement": "For the selected test data at a real place τ, suppose the cover Haar measure pushes forward to c₀μ, the Fock pairing comparison constant is C_F>0 and η=n·ι(κΦ) has norm one. The real local integral for measure μ equals C_F‖P_vη‖²/(c₀n²d)>0. The product of the real integrals is subsequently combined with the vacuum and product Haar constants.",
